{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["The sense of <b>I am YHWH your Elohim who brought you out of the land of Egypt</b> is that you were sojourners, and behold I gave you a possession. The meaning is joined to \"a sojourner and settler\" and \"he shall live with you,\" and also to the entire section mentioned concerning the redemption of the land. And he mentioned the section of \"and his hand shall be with you\" because the Israelite should bear in mind that he has great need, to the point that he sells himself — that he goes out in the jubilee. And behold the entire section of the parashah is joined together."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:27.250028399Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}